{"id": "EUVD-2026-98889", "enisaUuid": "2f54d518-d514-3e12-9944-1978f635f109", "description": "FastBee through 2.1.0 contains an insecure direct object reference vulnerability in DeviceController that allows authenticated low-privilege users to read and modify other tenants' devices by supplying sequential device IDs. Self-registered attackers can enumerate deviceId or serialNumber values to read owner, IP, and location data, and overwrite user_id and tenant_id to take over devices.", "datePublished": "2026-10-13T16:53:19", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-14T15:52:32", "baseScore": 8.6, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@1ExmmukzRMWN7B4gQ4W-4Q/fastbee-device-ownership-idor", "https://github.com/kerwincui/FastBee/blob/v2.1.0/springboot/fastbee-service/fastbee-iot-service/src/main/java/com/fastbee/iot/service/impl/DeviceServiceImpl.java#L105-L125", "https://github.com/kerwincui/FastBee/blob/v2.1.0/springboot/fastbee-open-api/src/main/java/com/fastbee/data/controller/DeviceController.java#L119-L211", "https://github.com/kerwincui/FastBee/blob/v1.2.1/springboot/wumei-iot/src/main/java/com/ruoyi/iot/controller/DeviceController.java#L118-L213", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/fastbee-through-2.1.0-idor-via-devicecontroller-iot-device-endpoints"], "aliases": ["GHSA-pv4m-4fcw-r33m", "CVE-2026-110124"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.3, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "946ecb01-c5ef-3b22-ac61-7729f5fefb61", "product": {"name": "FastBee", "vendor": {"name": "kerwincui"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22642.1.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "1a410e0e-3c47-382b-9db6-25a674a28c52", "vendor": {"name": "kerwincui"}}], "isExploited": false}